-> ownerId is the server-derived HMAC of (guest_id, guest's own stored token), NEVER the raw
   client-supplied guest_id, and the two guests' ownerIds are provably distinct (AC2).

Defense-in-depth / "ride the other guest's raw guest_id" attempt:
  Guest A's token + guest_id=910000037 (Guest B's id) in the request body
  -> HTTP 401 {"errors":"Unauthorized"} (APIGuestMiddleware/GuestTokenGuard token_mismatch,
     logged as [FAIL] guest.token.rejected, reason=token_mismatch, guest_id=910000037)
  -> resolveGuestOwnerKey is never even reached with a spoofed identity; middleware already
     blocks it upstream.
